<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to privatise tobacco curing company.</title>
<headline>Hungary to privatise tobacco curing company.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's state privatisation agency APV Rt said it will offer a 77.5 percent stake, representing a nominal value of 799.3 million forints ($5.1 million), in tobacco curing company Dohanyfermentalo Rt.</p>
<p>APV will try to find a strategic investor for 75 percent plus one share, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Thirty percent of the purchase price, but at least 60 million forints, is to be paid by cash in one instalment, while the rest can be paid with special coupons, it said.</p>
<p>Investors with more than a five percent stake in Hungarian tobacco product manufacturing may not participate, it said. ($ = 155.9 Hungarian Forints)</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
